  License: GPL (>= 2), as recorded in the archive's DESCRIPTION. The archive
  contains the complete upstream source and license metadata.
  Provenance and certified SHA-256:
    third_party/RCPP_SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md
  Homepage: https://www.rcpp.org

GNU/MinGW runtime libraries (binary artifacts when required)
  Windows builds made with GNU/MinGW may carry the recursively detected
  runtime DLL closure beside the extension or Stata plugin. Depending on the
  selected compiler this can include libgcc, libstdc++, libgomp, libatomic,
  libquadmath, libssp, and libwinpthread. Linux wheels repaired by auditwheel
  may likewise carry a private GNU runtime library needed by the extension.
  These files are copied unmodified from the compiler used for that artifact.

  GCC runtime libraries are distributed under GPLv3 with the GCC Runtime
  Library Exception 3.1 where stated by GCC. License information:
    https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/libstdc++/manual/license.html
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gcc-exception-3.1.html

  winpthreads is part of mingw-w64. Its upstream notice records copyright by
  the mingw-w64 project and Lockless Inc. and permissive MIT/BSD-style terms:
    https://github.com/mingw-w64/mingw-w64/blob/master/mingw-w64-libraries/winpthreads/COPYING

  Redistributors must retain the notices and license materials supplied with
  the exact compiler/runtime from which these binary files were taken.
